waiver: harness-limit
reason: the two interpreters keep a heap value as a value, not at an
  address, so a cast between an integer and a heap value has nothing to
  reinterpret there. The case runs on every compiled backend, where the
  cast reads and forges a real address. The interpreters still check the
  program, so E095 is pinned on them by diag_e095_pointer_cast_outside_unsafe.
